WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.240
This is part of a series I'm calling vlog extra days in April, which I hope you will join me...in...

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.580
Weird, weird, what is...

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.240
There's a, uh,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:16.920
little guy here. [Laughs] I think I accidentally just found a geocache. That's exactly what it is, and that's gross.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.760
It looks like there's some gross stuff in there. I'm going down to the river now.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.760
It's more of a creek, or as they say in Montana, "crick". I dunno why.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.580
Ooh! It's pretty.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.800
I'm basically just coming down here to find a nice place to film.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.999
So hopefully I will find one of those soon. I'm pretty good.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.880
Make sure my butt crack isn't showing.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.280
So I wanted to do something that no one had ever done before, an adaptation in online video.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.090
Taking a previous work  and transferring it into this new media.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.809
There's not...I don't know of any examples of this happening.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:53.660
I wanted something that was a great story that I loved, and I wanted to make this kind of something that my wife would really enjoy.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.100
And I wanted something that was very dialogue-based and very character-based,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.300
so that we could do it not as a big production with lots of sets and scenes and everything,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.840
but just as a person talking to a camera.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.150
It's a work of fiction,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.860
adapted into a video blog, and the work of fiction that we chose is Pride and Prejudice,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:16.520
because, you know, it's the best story of all time. Such a wonderful romance and the characters evolve so much,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.800
and I'm so interested in the—in this story, and I never would have been if it hadn't been for Katherine of course.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.360
But she's a huge P&amp;P fan.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.200
Basically a scholar.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.520
Its much, much different than anything I've ever done. When I make a video blog like I prefer to be alone, right?

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.560
This is like resting on a tree right now. Whereas this, you have to have actors and, like, a sound guy and

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:42.140
production people, and writers, and organizing all these people, and that's something that was totally new to me.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.800
And also like making a story, 'cause—'cause I feel like Vlogbrothers is a story, but it wasn't intentionally a story.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:53.680
We didn't set out to like, start here and end up here and have a middle. It's wonderful story, it's my favorite story ever,

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.920
but, with this, we're actually telling a story, we have to figure out how to break it up, and how to write it,

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.220
and how to transfer it into the present day, because obviously it's not a period piece.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.120
It's really new and really exciting for me to do something that-that's so different,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.461
and of course, like, I don't have time for this, but here I am doing it anyway,

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:13.120
because I was just so captured by the idea.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.920
And it's also important to note that it's very different from what I'm doing, and

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.620
thus it—I don't really know how to get it out there. There's part of me that's like, I know this is good...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.160
so what do I have to do now to actually get people to watch it?

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.440
We've made eight episodes, and to make more than eight episodes we're going to have to, you know,

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.620
somehow prove that people want to watch it, so either we can get a sponsor

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.600
or we could just get enough views that we can pay for it.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.980
It's pretty, you know, honestly dangerous because it's very different from the way that any other,

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:47.260
uh, fiction story has been told before, so it's entirely possible that it just will not be a good way to tell a story,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.900
and I hope that that's not the case,
I don't feel like that's the case,

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.840
but it-it's possible and that people won't react well to it.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:59.760
If you don't like it that's fine, and I'm not worried. It's-it-it's...I consider it to be an extremely exciting experiment.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.740
So that-that's how I'm feeling and I hope that, I hope that you like this...straight up

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.490
I hope that you like it.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:10.560
I hope that you enjoy it, and if you do, please share it, and hopefully, we can make this a sustainable project,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.160
and we'll get to tell the whole story of Lizzie Bennet, and Mr. Collins and Charlotte Lu...

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.680
Charlotte Lu, she's called Charlotte Lu in the show. Charlotte Lucas in the book.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.780
Now I have to go to a dinner party with some friends of mine.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:22.920
And now I'm home.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.077
Hey! That was a lovely dinner party. Look what my friend Dan got me.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.120
[singing] "Troy and Abed in the Moooorning!"

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.180
I'm gonna put an annotation up, so you could check out Lizzie Bennet Diaries,

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:36.640
John, you will see me tomorrow because I'm vlogging extra days in April. DFTBA.

